<section id="next" style="border-top: 1px solid #2E1F28">
<div style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 96px 24px">
<p style="margin: 0; font-family: Unbounded, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.24em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #F39C3D">After v0.1</p>
<h2 style="margin: 16px 0 0; max-width: 20em; font-family: Unbounded, sans-serif; font-weight: 500; font-size: clamp(28px, 3.4vw, 42px); line-height: 1.15">Where Mora goes next.</h2>
<p style="margin: 20px 0 0; max-width: 40em; color: #D9CCD3">The language is designed for these from the start, so they arrive without changing what you already wrote.</p>

<article style="margin-top: 48px; border-radius: 16px; border: 1px solid #4A0E3B; background: #1A0D15; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; overflow: hidden">
<div style="flex: 1 1 340px; min-width: 0; padding: 28px">
<span style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 999px; background: #3A1530; color: #FFD27A">v0.3</span>
<h3 style="margin: 14px 0 8px; font-size: 21px; font-weight: 600">Contracts and property tests</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; color: #B8A9B1">A <code>contract</code> section states each member's rules away from the signature: invariants, preconditions, declared failures and postconditions. Property tests are generated from the same rules, with shrinking on failure.</p>
</div>
<div style="flex: 1 1 520px; min-width: 0; background: #0D0709; overflow-x: auto; padding: 24px">
<pre style="font-size: 13px">    <span class="k">contract</span> &#123;
        <span class="k">invariant</span> Balance &gt;= 0;

        Withdraw &#123;
            <span class="k">fails with</span> <span class="t">AccountError</span>.Frozen <span class="k">when</span> IsFrozen;
            <span class="k">fails with</span> <span class="t">AccountError</span>.Insufficient <span class="k">when</span> amount &gt; Balance;
            <span class="k">ensures</span> Balance == old(Balance) - amount;
        &#125;
    &#125;</pre>
</div>
</article>

<div style="margin-top: 20px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(260px, 100%), 1fr)); gap: 20px">
<article style="padding: 24px; border-radius: 16px; border: 1px solid #33232D; background: #180E13">
<span style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 999px; background: #2A1C24; color: #FFD27A">v0.2</span>
<h3 style="margin: 14px 0 6px; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600">Libraries as WebAssembly</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; color: #B8A9B1">A library ships as one <code>.wasm</code> file with its metadata and typed IR, for wasm and native programs alike. Plugins load natively or sandboxed from one interface.</p>
</article>
<article style="padding: 24px; border-radius: 16px; border: 1px solid #33232D; background: #180E13">
<span style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 999px; background: #2A1C24; color: #FFD27A">v0.2</span>
<h3 style="margin: 14px 0 6px; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600">Capability grants</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; color: #B8A9B1">Give each dependency only the capabilities it needs, checked from inferred effects, and run programs in a sandbox that enforces them.</p>
</article>
<article style="padding: 24px; border-radius: 16px; border: 1px solid #33232D; background: #180E13">
<span style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 999px; background: #2A1C24; color: #FFD27A">v0.2</span>
<h3 style="margin: 14px 0 6px; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600">Tools for agents</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; color: #B8A9B1"><code>mora mcp</code> serves queries, context, checks and fixes to coding agents. Mark a function <code>@Tool</code> and its signature becomes an MCP tool.</p>
</article>
<article style="padding: 24px; border-radius: 16px; border: 1px solid #33232D; background: #180E13">
<span style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 999px; background: #2A1C24; color: #FFD27A">v0.2</span>
<h3 style="margin: 14px 0 6px; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600">Semver the compiler checks</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; color: #B8A9B1"><code>mora diff</code> reports the smallest version bump a change needs, and <code>mora publish</code> refuses one that is too small.</p>
</article>
<article style="padding: 24px; border-radius: 16px; border: 1px solid #33232D; background: #180E13">
<span style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 999px; background: #2A1C24; color: #FFD27A">v0.3</span>
<h3 style="margin: 14px 0 6px; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600">Simulation, replay, hot reload</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; color: #B8A9B1">Test against a simulated world with a virtual clock and injected faults, record a run and replay it, and swap changed functions into a running program.</p>
</article>
<article style="padding: 24px; border-radius: 16px; border: 1px solid #33232D; background: #180E13">
<span style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 999px; background: #2A1C24; color: #FFD27A">v0.3</span>
<h3 style="margin: 14px 0 6px; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600">Units of measure</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; color: #B8A9B1">Dimensions multiply and divide, so <code>Meters / Seconds</code> is a speed, and the cost falls only on code that declares units.</p>
</article>
<article style="padding: 24px; border-radius: 16px; border: 1px solid #33232D; background: #180E13">
<span style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 999px; background: #2A1C24; color: #FFD27A">v0.4</span>
<h3 style="margin: 14px 0 6px; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600">Threads</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; color: #B8A9B1"><code>shared</code> classes, <code>Mutex</code>, <code>Channel</code> and a multi-threaded executor, with sendability checked at compile time.</p>
</article>
<article style="padding: 24px; border-radius: 16px; border: 1px solid #33232D; background: #180E13">
<span style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 999px; background: #2A1C24; color: #FFD27A">v0.5</span>
<h3 style="margin: 14px 0 6px; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600">Registry and more targets</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; color: #B8A9B1">A package registry with signed publishing, an LLVM release backend, and embedded devices with no OS.</p>
</article>
</div>
</div>
